+	// A prepared tree already holds everything the conversion would produce, so there is nothing to
+	// convert - and no original game files to ask for, they are not deployed with such a tree. That also
+	// means none of the checks in RefreshCache() can run, so the tree carries a record of what it was
+	// built against and this compares the two numbers those checks would have compared.
+	std::uint32_t treeCacheVersion = 0, treeEventCount = 0;
